ing if there are any common factors between the numerator and denominator.\n\nTesting 31,579 for divisibility: it's odd, the digit sum is 25 (not divisible by 3), doesn't end in 0 or 5, and checking 7, 11, and 13 all fail. Rather than continue factoring, I'll proceed with direct division. Let me test 486,000,000 as a candidate by computing 31,579 × 486 = 31,579 × (500 - 14) = 15,789,500 - 442,106 = 15,347,394.\n\nScaling up: 31,579 × 486,000,000 = 15,347,394,000,000. Since 15,330,999,751,182 is less than this, the quotient must be smaller. Testing 485,500,000 instead: 31,579 × 485,500 = 31,579 × 485,000 + 31,579 × 500 = 15,315,815,000 + 15,789,500 = 15,331,604,500, so 31,579 × 485,500,000 = 15,331,604,500,000. This is still larger than the target, so I need to go lower, around 485,480,000.\n\nComputing 31,579 × 485,480 by subtracting 20 from the previous result: 15,331,604,500 - 631,580 = 15,330,972,920, giving 31,579 × 485,480,000 = 15,330,972,920,000. The remainder is 26,831,182. Breaking this down further: 31,579 × 800 = 25,263,200 leaves 1,567,982, then 31,579 × 49 = 1,547,371 leaves 20,611. The final quotient is 485,480,849 with remainder 20,611.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19263,"cache_read_input_tokens":20965,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19263},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"63f2ae24-fc3d-3348-008d-4127610461e3","uuid":"5002cd7b-93de-4583-a5a4-7731deadee7a"}
